  "body": "## What changed\n\nLathe tools now have their own cutting-data model: surface speed (Vc) and feed per rev, with a max-rpm clamp. Turning ops suggest S/F from it and post G96 under that clamp.\n\n- **Turning table** (`crates/tools/src/turning_data.rs`, new): Vc (m/min) and f (mm/rev) ranges for each work material, for HSS and carbide. These are our own conservative starting values, inside the ranges that Machinery's Handbook-style turning tables print (provenance comment). Grooving blades and form gauges take 0.4 x the feed. Boring bars take 0.8 x both Vc and feed.\n- **`Tool::turning: Option<TurningData>`** `{ vc, feed_per_rev, max_rpm }`. It is checked by `Tool::is_sane`: values must be finite and in bounds, and the tool's constant rpm must not be above its own clamp. The project file and catalog key `turning` is additive and only written when stated, so old project and tool files load unchanged (pinned).\n- **Suggestion** (`crates/app/src/cutting_turn.rs`, new, plus `cutting::suggest` handing off to it):\n  - Covers every turning op except Threading, which keeps a constant rpm for the synchronized pass.\n  - Vc and f/rev are the window middles.\n  - The rpm is read at the stock's swing diameter about the spindle axis (program Z through the WCS origin, the lathe posts' meridian law). It is held to the tool's max rpm, then the machine's spindle max. If it falls under the machine's minimum the suggestion is refused, not raised.\n  - Feed = f x rpm and plunge = f/2 x rpm (mm/min, not rounded), so the post's `F = feed / rpm` is exactly the table's f/rev.\n- **`ApplyCuttingData`** writes the op's feed and plunge, and the tool's rpm and turning data, as one undo unit. The tool's own clamp is kept. This uses the existing `EditOperationParams` + `ChangeTool` composite, so there is no new command.\n- **Posting**:\n  - A CSS-eligible op whose tool states turning data puts `PARAM SurfaceSpeed <Vc>` on the stream, and also `PARAM MaxSpindleSpeed <rpm>` when the tool states a clamp (`post::Dump::css`).\n  - `fanuc-lathe.cps` writes `G50 S<min(machine, tool)>` before the G96 when that clamp is not already in force. Before a later G97 section it lifts the clamp back to the machine's.\n  - `tormach-lathe.cps` writes `G96 D<min(machine, tool)>`.\n  - **Both posts now refuse, by name, a G96 when neither the machine nor the tool states a maximum rpm.** Before this PR, Tormach posted a G96 with no D and Fanuc posted one with no G50.\n  - Tools without turning data post byte-identically (G97).\n- **UI**:\n  - New tool-editor rows (`tool_turning_row.rs`) for lathe steels: state turning data, Vc (m/min, or ft/min in an inch document), f/rev, and max rpm. The values ride the existing `ChangeTool` Apply.\n  - The Feeds page readout shows \"Vc · f/rev at Ø D\" for a turning suggestion.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/891-lathe-cutting-data.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nCarbide on mild steel, 12 mm bar: Vc 170 m/min, f 0.2 mm/rev, 170000/(pi*12) = 4509 rpm, feed 901.8 mm/min, plunge 450.9 mm/min. The posted program reads `G50 S12000`, `G96 S170 M03`, cuts at `F0.2` and plunges at `F0.1` (G99).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/lathe_post_css.rs` (new):\n- `a_turning_op_on_mild_steel_gets_the_table_vc_and_feed_per_rev`\n- `applying_the_turning_suggestion_is_one_undo_and_posts_g96_and_the_table_feed`: pinned on the new golden `golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/facing_css.nc`\n- `a_tool_max_rpm_holds_the_suggestion_and_clamps_both_dialects`: `G50 S3000` + `G96 S170`, Tormach `G96 D3000`\n- `a_g96_with_no_clamp_anywhere_is_refused_by_name`: both dialects\n- `a_tool_without_turning_data_posts_g97_and_threading_never_runs_css`\n- `turning_data_is_additive_in_the_project_file_and_sanity_checked`: old tool has no key, stated data round-trips byte-identically, bad values are refused\n\nUnit tests:\n- `camcraft-tools` `turning_data::tests`: table order, rpm hand calculation, sanity bounds\n- `camcraft-ui` `tool_turning_row::tests::the_editor_draft_carries_the_turning_data_through_apply`\n\nQuick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on this head: tools, post, motion, app (every suite, since a new golden file counts as shared test input) and ui, 0 failed, 27.5 min wall. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens\n\n- New: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/facing_css.nc`.\n- None moved: the starter catalog states no turning data, so every existing lathe golden still posts G97.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The new tool-editor rows and the Feeds-page readout have not been driven in a live GUI. Only the draft round-trip is unit-tested, and no snapshot PNG changed.\n- The inch (ft/min, in/rev) display lens on those rows is not exercised.\n- Grooving, form and boring factors are not pinned by their own end-to-end post tests. Only the facing path is.\n\n## Overlap\n\n`assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` and `tormach-lathe.cps` are touched only in the spindle preamble, `onParameter` and `endPreamble`. The threading code is not touched. Draft PRs #516/#517/#518/#468 edit threading in the same files, so a textual merge-of-main may be needed, but there is no logic overlap.\n\n## MCP\n\nNo new command. `add_tool` / `set_tool` take the tool definition JSON (the project `ToolDto`), so the new `turning` key is available there already. The MCP tool for `ApplyCuttingData` is still owed by the existing #732 (P1, area:mcp), which now also covers turning ops.\n\nChangelog: Turning: lathe tools state surface speed, feed per rev and a max-rpm clamp; turning ops suggest S/F from a turning table and post G96 under a G50/D clamp, and an unclamped G96 is refused by name (#891)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #891\n",
